cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these datasets or this code, please cite the release and
  the accompanying article.
title: >-
  Explainable machine learning surrogates for structural simulation:
  benchmark datasets and code
authors:
  - family-names: Jha
    given-names: Rishav
    affiliation: MIT Campus, Rajarshi Janak University, Janakpurdham, Nepal
  - family-names: Sahani
    given-names: Suresh Kumar
    email: sureshsahani54@gmail.com
    affiliation: MIT Campus, Rajarshi Janak University, Janakpurdham, Nepal
  - family-names: Sahani
    given-names: Kameshwar
    affiliation: Department of Civil Engineering, Kathmandu University, Dhulikhel, Nepal
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-25'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/jharishav036-gif/structural-surrogate-benchmark'
abstract: >-
  Parameterized benchmark datasets and the complete analysis code for a
  study of nine regression models used as surrogates for finite-element
  structural simulation (cantilever beam, fixed-base portal frame,
  six-panel Pratt truss). Includes solver verification against
  closed-form solutions, stratified splits, 10-fold cross-validation,
  held-out and extrapolation evaluation, SHAP interpretability analysis
  compared with solver-based sensitivity indices, Friedman and
  Holm-corrected statistical comparisons, learning curves, a
  solver-versus-surrogate timing benchmark, and a 100,000-candidate
  design-screening study with conformal uncertainty intervals.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - surrogate models
  - structural analysis
  - finite element method
  - SHAP
  - explainability
  - benchmark
